From: CodeAndSolder <codeandsolder@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ubus: annotate intentional notification fallthrough

Non-channel notifications and unsubscriptions intentionally share the
invoke path. Mark this branch explicitly for GCC/Clang with strict
implicit-fallthrough warnings, preserving the channel-specific break.

---
--- a/libubus.c
+++ b/libubus.c
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
 	case UBUS_MSG_NOTIFY:
 		if (ubus_context_is_channel(ctx))
 			break;
-		/* fallthrough */
+		fallthrough;
 	case UBUS_MSG_INVOKE:
 		if (ctx->stack_depth) {
 			ubus_queue_msg(ctx, buf);
